704. Binary Search

Description:
Given a sorted array nums and a target, find the index of the target using Binary Search. If the target is not present, return -1.

The algorithm must run in O(log n) time.

Test Case:

Input:  nums = [-1,0,3,5,9,12], target = 9
Output: 4

Why?
9 is present in the array at index 4, so we return 4.

class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        int low=0, high=nums.length-1;
        while(low<=high){
            int mid = low+(high-low)/2;
            if(nums[mid]==target){
                return mid;
            }else if(target<nums[mid]){
                high=mid-1;
            }else if(target>nums[mid]){
                low=mid+1;
            }
        }
        return -1;
    }
}
